Sun Aug 30 15:18:26 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Require nlohmann_json in -devel: libsigmfConfig.cmake does
  find_dependency() on it, so find_package(libsigmf) failed for
  every consumer that did not already pull it in
- Add libsigmf-install-interface-include-path.patch: the installed
  CMake interface exposed only <prefix>/include, so the usage the
  README documents, #include <sigmf.h>, did not compile (nor did
  the angle-bracket include inside flatbuffers_type_to_json.h)
- Run upstream's example programs in %check instead of leaving it
  empty; they are the only thing that compiles a header-only
  library, and one of them checks a full JSON round-trip:
  * build them with -UNDEBUG: their asserts are the entire
    verification, and compiled out they report success no matter
    what the code did
  * also build and run a throwaway consumer against the staged
    tree, so a broken installed CMake config fails here rather
    than in every consumer
- Ship NOTICE next to LICENSE (Apache-2.0 attribution)
- Spec cleanup: %autosetup, summary/description that describe SigMF
  rather than repeating the package name

